  "surprise": "Recompile storm despite dynamic=True: 003's failure again, now at 40-55 s per compile because the graph holds forward+backward of seven 384-wide blocks. Metric 162 (485/0/0) vs 153's 687 (676/700/685), -525; seeds 1 and 2 handed off an untrained model. Every mechanism prediction failed: unique_graphs 8/26/25 (registered 1; the >=3 falsifier fired on all seeds), steps 1292/7/15 (registered 4,600-5,600; falsifier <4,400), first step at 81/75/81 s (setup 15 s + ~65 s first compile). Cause, from the pod logs (torch 2.4.0): the compiled mtp_loss frame was specialized on the batch's padded length despite dynamic=True ('L[m] size mismatch at index 1, expected 166, actual 92'), and after the cache_size_limit=2 fuse dropped that frame to eager, Dynamo kept intercepting the NESTED frames (ALiBiGPT.features, PeriLNBlock.forward, PeriLNBlock.attn) as separate compile units, each with Inductor's ambient alignment guards (Mod(T,8)==0, Mod(T^2,8)==0, T==B, mask.stride()[2]==B), so a new (B,T) still meant a new 40-55 s compile ('[2/14]' = the 14th compile of PeriLNBlock.forward); the per-frame limit did not stop it. Seed 0 happened to exhaust its variants by ~205 s and then ran ~1,290 eager steps in the last ~95 s (13.6 steps/s, the incumbent's eager rate; val loss 0.085 at 300 s, greedy 0.889 after 1.15 epochs, RL r1 365/1500 at acc 0.055, r4 956, eval 485); seeds 1 and 2 compiled on every step (7 and 15 steps, val loss 4.45/3.93, greedy 0.0, 0 solved, totals 1382/1463 s). The local CPU check (torch 2.14) that served seven shapes with one graph did not transfer: the guards are torch-2.4 and CUDA/SDPA specific. Lesson for the speed lane: on this pod image, compile only with a FIXED padded shape (pad every batch to constant T and constant record count, i.e. give up token-budget batching or pad to a small set of shapes and compile each once, ~50 s each), or upgrade the pod's torch before trying dynamic shapes; the throughput of a compiled step was never observed, so the lead is still unmeasured. The 90 s bench never returned a result line (its pod took >14 min to provision and the captured output was empty), so this registration went out without a probe; the fuse design was the error, not the missing probe.",
